    "q-105654": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105654",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨y{e}^{-x},-y{e}^{y}⟩$ and $f(x,y)=x,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨1,0⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{-x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-y{e}^{y})=-y{e}^{-x}-{e}^{y}-y{e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =x(-y{e}^{-x}-{e}^{y}-y{e}^{y})+⟨y{e}^{-x},-y{e}^{y}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =-yx{e}^{-x}-x{e}^{y}-yx{e}^{y}+y{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =y{e}^{-x}-yx{e}^{-x}-x{e}^{y}-yx{e}^{y} \\\\  & =y(1-x){e}^{-x}-x(1+y){e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
