    "q-131243": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131243",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Calculate $∇\\cdot (-4F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF={x}^{2}yz\\,i+({y}^{3}-y)\\,j-xy{z}^{2}\\,k.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (-4F)=-4∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}-y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-xy{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xyz+3{y}^{2}-1-2xyz \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (-4F) & =-4∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (3{y}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =4-12{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-131243-a",
