    "q-131291": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131291",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,x{z}^{3},{z}^{2}⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2xz,0,{x}^{2}⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{z}^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})=\\frac{1}{x}+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & ={x}^{2}z(\\frac{1}{x}+2z)+⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,x{z}^{3},{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2xz,0,{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =xz+2{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{2}{z}^{2} \\\\  & =xz+3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =xz(1+3xz+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
